      "claim": "A rational consumer chooses the quantity of a good that maximizes net benefit, defined as total benefit minus total cost.",
      "evidence": "Standard micro‑economic theory of consumer choice; the consumer is assumed to be utility‑maximizing and to compare marginal changes in benefit and cost.",
